r=items['ex-sr-rindler-wedge-congruence-worked'];st=r['statement'].replace('on (0,inf)xR^3','on R x (0,inf) x R^2, with theta in R and rho>0').replace('= -(1/rho^2) partial_theta = -(1/rho) n','= +(1/rho^2) partial_theta = +(1/rho) n');strategy=r['strategy']+' In the bracket, partial_rho(rho^-1)=-rho^-2 and the convention [f partial_theta,partial_rho]=-partial_rho(f)partial_theta gives the positive sign.';propose(r['id'],st,strategy)
b=items['ex-sr-bell-congruence-fails-born-rigidity'];st=b['statement'].replace("|q_1'(t)| = alpha t < c","|q_1'(t)| = alpha |t| < c").replace('(2 + gamma^2 alpha^2t^2/c^2) gamma^3 alpha^2 t/c^3','gamma^3 alpha^2 t/c^3');strategy="Put beta=alpha t/c and beta'=alpha/c. With x^0=ct, partial_0 n_0=-gamma^3 alpha^2t/c^3 and partial_0 n_1=gamma^3 alpha/c^2. Contract with s=(gamma alpha t/c,gamma,0,0): theta(s,s)=gamma^5 alpha^2t(1-alpha^2t^2/c^2)/c^3=gamma^3 alpha^2t/c^3. This vanishes exactly at t=0 on the two-sided subluminal domain |t|<c/alpha. At c=1, beta=3/5 and beta'=1 the general contraction is75/64, while the discarded extra factor gives3075/1024. The translated members differ by the constant vector xi_1-xi_2 at a fixed chart time. No elasticity or breaking conclusion is drawn.";propose(b['id'],st,strategy)
