ce=items['cex-sr-born-rigid-motion-need-not-be-killing'];st='''Statement refuted: 'every smooth Born-rigid future unit timelike field n is locally a positive multiple of a Killing field'. Fix a length scale L_0>0 and use a geometric proper-length parameter lambda (the model's proper-time parameter is tau=lambda/c). Put psi(lambda)=lambda^2/(2L_0^2), e_0(lambda)=(cosh psi,sinh psi,0,0), e_1(lambda)=(sinh psi,cosh psi,0,0), and z(lambda)=(integral_0^lambda cosh psi(s) ds,integral_0^lambda sinh psi(s) ds,0,0), so z'=e_0 and eta(z',z')=-1. Define Phi(lambda,xi,y,zeta)=z(lambda)+xi e_1(lambda)+y e_2+zeta e_3. On a sufficiently small open coordinate box around0 this is injective with smooth inverse and N=1+k(lambda)xi>0, where k(lambda)=lambda/L_0^2; its pullback metric is -N^2 d lambda^2+d xi^2+dy^2+d zeta^2. The unit field n=N^-1 partial_lambda is future, irrotational and Born rigid: its rest slices lambda=const have fixed Euclidean induced metric. Its acceleration one-form is a-flat=[k(lambda)/N]d xi, and d(a-flat)=[1/(L_0^2N^2)]d lambda wedge d xi is nowhere zero. For a positive smooth f, the Killing equation for K=f n and Born rigidity imply d log f=a-flat, impossible because d^2 log f=0. Thus no positive smooth multiple of this n is Killing even locally; irrotational Born rigidity does not force a Killing rescaling. The Rindler congruence is not this counterexample: rho n=partial_theta is Killing for its theta-independent metric. The rotational classification of thm-sr-smooth-local-herglotz-noether is preserved; this example concerns its irrotational branch.'''
